{"The cache key generated by `userPermDenialCacheKey` overlaps with the keyspace of `userPermCacheKey`. This causes collisions if an `action` contains underscores (e.g., `action=\"read_name_parent\"` vs `action=\"read\"` with `name=\"name\"`). Use a unique prefix for denial keys, such as `.perm_denial_`, to ensure keyspace isolation and prevent incorrect cache results or invalidations.": 0.565760612487793, "The denial cache key is built without `IdentityType`, so a deny cached for one identity type (e.g., user vs service account) can incorrectly deny another with the same UID. Include identity type in the cache key to avoid cross-identity contamination.": 0.7352473735809326}